---
// Privacy notice. Company facts come from site.ts; an empty value renders nothing.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, formatDate } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'why-we-use-it', title: 'Why we use it and the legal bases' },
  { id: 'who-processes-it', title: 'Who processes it' },
  { id: 'international-transfers', title: 'International transfers' },
  { id: 'retention', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'complaints', title: 'Complaints' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes' },
];

const domain = site.url.replace('https://', '');
const mailto = `mailto:${site.email}`;
const registration =
  `The company is registered in ${site.country}` +
  (site.croNumber ? `, company number ${site.croNumber}` : '') +
  (site.registeredOffice ? `, with its registered office at ${site.registeredOffice}` : '') +
  '.';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy notice: Viaclin"
  description="How Viaclin Limited handles personal data on viaclin.com: the contact form, analytics by consent, who processes it, retention, your rights and how to complain."
  lead="What this website collects, why, who handles it, how long it stays and the rights you hold."
  path="/privacy"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}, trading as {site.name}, is the data controller for this website. {registration}
  </p>
  <p>
    This notice covers {domain} and the enquiries that reach us through it. It follows the General Data Protection
    Regulation (GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018. Work we carry out for a client is covered by the contract for
    that engagement.
  </p>
  <p>For any question about this notice or your data, write to <a href={mailto}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>

  <h3>When you send the contact form</h3>
  <p>
    We receive your name, company, work email, programme stage and message, along with a record that you ticked the
    consent box.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form also carries campaign values, such as utm_source, where the address of the page holds them, along with
    the path of that page. If you have accepted analytics, the site keeps those values for the rest of your visit, so
    the form carries the ones from the page you landed on.
  </p>
  <p>If you write to us by email instead, we hold your address and whatever you choose to tell us.</p>
  <p>
    The site does not ask for health data or any other special category of data. Leave patient and trial subject
    details out of your message.
  </p>

  <h3>When you visit</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider records standard server logs, including IP address, browser type, the page requested and the
    time of the request, to run and protect the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site also keeps a small number of settings in your browser, such as your light or dark theme. The
    {' '}<a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> lists each one.
  </p>

  <h3>When you accept analytics or insights</h3>
  <p>
    Nothing in this group loads until you say yes. Google Consent Mode starts every visit with all signals set to
    denied, and the advertising signals stay denied whatever you choose.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics.</strong> Google Analytics 4 records the pages you view, the site or campaign that brought you
      here, your device and browser type, an approximate location taken from your IP address, and events such as a
      button press, a form start or a search.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Insights.</strong> Microsoft Clarity records how pages are used: clicks, taps, scrolling and pointer
      movement. We see the results as heatmaps and session replays. With the same consent, the site can place you in a
      test group so that we can compare two versions of a page.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use these tools to see how the site performs, not to work out who you are. The site carries no advertising, and
    we do not sell data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="why-we-use-it">Why we use it and the legal bases</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Purposes and legal bases">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Data</th>
          <th scope="col">Legal basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Reply to your enquiry and, where you ask us to, prepare a proposal</td>
          <td>Contact form and email details</td>
          <td>Your consent, given when you tick the box and send the form: Article 6(1)(a) GDPR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Measure how the site is used, so that we can improve it</td>
          <td>Analytics data</td>
          <td>Your consent, given through the cookie settings: Article 6(1)(a) GDPR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>See how pages are used and compare page versions</td>
          <td>Insights data</td>
          <td>Your consent, given through the cookie settings: Article 6(1)(a) GDPR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Run the site, keep it secure and investigate misuse</td>
          <td>Server logs</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interest in a working, secure website: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    You can withdraw consent at any time. For analytics and insights, open the cookie settings from the footer of any
    page or from the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>. For an enquiry, email us. Withdrawal does not affect
    anything done before it.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are under no duty to give us data. Without a name and an email address we cannot reply to an enquiry. We make
    no decisions about you by automated means.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-processes-it">Who processes it</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of providers to run the site. The privacy notice of each one explains how it handles data.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Providers that process data">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Provider</th>
          <th scope="col">What it does for us</th>
          <th scope="col">Data</th>
          <th scope="col">When</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel</a></th>
          <td>Hosts and delivers the site</td>
          <td>Server logs, including IP address</td>
          <td>On every visit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a></th>
          <td>Passes contact form submissions to our mailbox</td>
          <td>The contents of the form</td>
          <td>When you send the form</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics 4</a></th>
          <td>Site measurement</td>
          <td>Analytics data</td>
          <td>After you accept analytics</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Clarity</a></th>
          <td>Heatmaps and session replays</td>
          <td>Insights data</td>
          <td>After you accept insights</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Enquiries arrive in our business mailbox, which an email provider hosts for us.</p>
  <p>
    We disclose data to a court, a regulator or a professional adviser where the law requires it, or where we need to
    establish or defend a legal claim. We do not sell data, and we do not pass it to anyone for their marketing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Vercel, Web3Forms, Google and Microsoft may process data in the United States and in other countries outside the
    European Economic Area.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where that happens, the transfer rests on one of two safeguards: the European Commission's adequacy decision for
    the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, for providers certified under it, or the Commission's standard contractual
    clauses. Email us if you would like to know which safeguard covers a given provider.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries:</strong>{' '}
      {site.enquiryRetention
        ? `${site.enquiryRetention}, or longer where the enquiry becomes part of an engagement record.`
        : 'for as long as it takes to answer you and, where work follows, for as long as the engagement record is kept.'}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics and insights:</strong> the settings of each provider decide. We set Google Analytics 4 to its
      14 month option for user and event data. Microsoft Clarity keeps recordings and heatmap data for the periods in
      its own documentation.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> held by our hosting provider under its own schedule.</li>
    <li><strong>Browser storage:</strong> the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> gives the life of each item.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>At the end of a period we delete the data or anonymise it.</p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you a copy of the data we hold about you</li>
    <li>correct data that is wrong or incomplete</li>
    <li>erase your data</li>
    <li>restrict how we use it</li>
    <li>send it to you, or to another organisation, in a portable format</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also object to processing that rests on our legitimate interests, and you can withdraw consent at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, email <a href={mailto}>{site.email}</a>. We may ask for proof of identity before we
    act. We answer within one month. The law allows two further months for a complex request, and we will tell you if
    we need them. There is no charge for a request. The law allows a fee, or a refusal, where a request is unfounded or
    excessive.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaints">Complaints</h2>
  <p>If something has gone wrong, tell us first at <a href={mailto}>{site.email}</a> and we will try to put it right.</p>
  <p>
    You have the right to complain to the Data Protection Commission, the supervisory authority for Ireland, at
    {' '}<a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener noreferrer">dataprotection.ie</a>. If you live or work in
    another EU or EEA country, you can complain to the authority there instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is written for people who work in life sciences companies. It is not aimed at children, and we do not
    seek data from anyone under 18. If you believe a child has sent us data, tell us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This notice was last updated on {formatDate(site.legalUpdated)}. Changes appear on this page, and the date at the
    top shows when the text last changed.
  </p>
</Legal>

<style>
  /* provider names stay on one line; the table scrolls inside its frame on a narrow screen */
  tbody th {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
